; The transcripts of 'humpty expect'. The cpu binary, because no model is
; loaded and the backend does not show in a transcript.

(cram
 (package humpty)
 (deps %{bin:humpty-cpu}))

; A transcript whose okit is active names on its status line whether an
; ocamlmerlin answered for the workspace, so these need one to be installed and
; not only the merlin scenarios do. The other two record a workspace okit
; refused and one it was never asked about, neither of which mentions merlin.
;
; humpty builds and runs in a switch without merlin, which is why the gate is
; here at all. humpty's test dependencies name merlin, so it is there wherever
; the suite is meant to run and the gate never fires.

(cram
 (package humpty)
 (applies_to basic diagnostics promote merlin)
 (enabled_if %{bin-available:ocamlmerlin}))
